      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A single dose is usually 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest common tablet strength. This dose is about twice the maximum. It carries a serious risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day total, so the \"1700\" may have been the daily total.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- **A lower starting dose.** If the patient is metformin-naive, the usual start is 500 mg once or twice daily, titrated up.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. I'll enter it once you do. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please have the supervising physician confirm it first."
      }
     ],
